From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Jones <grahamjonesgs@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:39:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ldso: support an ELF class narrower than the pointer size

An arch whose reloc.h defines DL_ELFCLASS 32 while its pointers are 64
bits (KlaussCPU: LP64 C in ELFCLASS32 files) has a dynamic section and
REL/RELA tables of 32-bit words, sign-extended r_addend and 32-bit
.gnu.hash Bloom words, while the fields that relocations write (GOT
entries, data pointers, TLS offsets and module IDs) and the aux vector
stay size_t.

dynlink.h selects Ehdr/Phdr/Sym and R_TYPE/R_SYM/R_INFO from
DL_ELFCLASS (after reloc.h, so the arch can set it; an arch's own
R_TYPE still wins) and adds Word/Sword, the type of a dynamic-section
or relocation-table element. For every arch whose class matches its
pointer size, Word is size_t and Sword ptrdiff_t, DL_ELF_NARROW is 0
and the generated code is unchanged.

dynlink.c and dlstart.c read the dynamic section through
decode_dynv/search_dynv (decode_vec/search_vec unless narrow), walk the
relocation tables as Word arrays and sign-extend r_addend, size the
.gnu.hash Bloom words as Word, and keep the lazy relocation copies as
Word triples. ELFCLASS32 RELR cannot describe size_t fields, so a
narrow arch reports it as unsupported and _dlstart skips it.
